{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1343159-mage-arena","id":1343159,"title":"Mage Arena","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-23T06:57:39-07:00","id":1343159,"title":"Mage Arena","content":"I saw this on the Exalted forum and wanted to transfer the idea here. Since there is tremendous variations among Mages, I wonder how they would fare in an arena setting. Sure Mages tend to be scholars but I am sure they can apply their magic to combat. How would mages fare against...<br /> <br /> 1) mage vs mage fights? This can also put pentacle mages against the minions of the seers of the throne.<br /> <br /> 2) mage vs other supernatural creatures such as a fight between a mage against a vampire, promethean, changeling, or werewolf?<br /> <br /> 3) mage vs an Antagonist such as a Spirit or something like a Idigam? I am sure the antagonists from other game lines can port nicely to Mage before their antagonist book comes out.<br /> <br /> the Exalted forum seems to support this discussion, I wonder how it translates to other game lines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T10:06:32-07:00","id":1343203,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a perennial topic for some reason.<br /> <br /> Mages would be fine at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T10:53:32-07:00","id":1343214,"title":"","content":"The general consensus tends to be that it depends on the context. Mages don't lend themselves much to white room scenarios. They will try to prepare for a problem or sidestep it entirely. They are very squishy, so creating the most asymmetrical scenario possible is the most reliable way to ensure victory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T11:25:01-07:00","id":1343224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1343159-mage-arena#post1343159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this on the Exalted forum and wanted to transfer the idea here. Since there is tremendous variations among Mages, I wonder how they would fare in an arena setting. Sure Mages tend to be scholars but I am sure they can apply their magic to combat. How would mages fare against...<br /> <br /> 1) mage vs mage fights? This can also put pentacle mages against the minions of the seers of the throne.<br /> <br /> 2) mage vs other supernatural creatures such as a fight between a mage against a vampire, promethean, changeling, or werewolf?<br /> <br /> 3) mage vs an Antagonist such as a Spirit or something like a Idigam? I am sure the antagonists from other game lines can port nicely to Mage before their antagonist book comes out.<br /> <br /> the Exalted forum seems to support this discussion, I wonder how it translates to other game lines</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1343159-mage-arena?p=1343214#post1343214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general consensus tends to be that it depends on the context. Mages don't lend themselves much to white room scenarios. They will try to prepare for a problem or sidestep it entirely. They are very squishy, so creating the most asymmetrical scenario possible is the most reliable way to ensure victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Master of Life and Mind, is potentially a combat monster.<br /> <br /> Turn 1: They hide themself for the scene with a Veiling Life spell<br /> Turn 2: Veil their Mind to prevent opponents from using Theory of Mind ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theory_of_mind\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theory_of_mind</a> ) to guess at what they might do or where they might go.<br /> Next Several Turns: Buff themself like crazy, and give themself natural weapons like huge claws or something<br /> Proceed to kill their opponents so hard with buckets of dice.<br /> <br /> Alternatively: A Master of Death says &quot;they're dead now&quot;, and the universe says &quot;ok&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: For the Life+Mind example, spell control limits on all those buffs aren't a problem, they can just set the duration to less than the minimum time for an unsafely relinquished spell to go wrong, unsafely relinquish the buffs with Willpower Points, then restore their own Willpower with spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-23-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T13:11:23-07:00","id":1343255,"title":"","content":"Mage battles tend to be all or nothing. Ive very rarely had a battle last past the second round. Without rules and limitations, or a point system, like the Duel Arcane, then Mages tend to solve battles with their first spell or second spell.<br /> <br /> In my Mage setting, I actually do have a &quot;Mage Arena&quot;, led by literally just the Black Black club from Yu Yu Hakusho, Sakkyo and all, here he is a Left-Handed Seer of the Throne who has grown bored in his dominion, and uses his illegal underground monster arena and betting to entertain himself, and uses the arena as a means of punishment, execution, or even just hazing, toward other Mages, even other Seers in the case of hazing. His Arena has stone tablets that act as &quot;game modes&quot; with carefully programmed imbued effects, such as one that casts a Wards and Signs that selectively prohibits certain practices or Arcana to prevent fights ending too quickly, or at least make it harder to succeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just off the top of my head, though, I could see the Arrows forming sparring and training grounds where Mages duel each other regularly, refining the Adamant Hand or trying to integrate hurt locker merits into their Shadow Names, and such.<br /> <br /> A modified Duel Arcane system, and or hosting Mage Arena in the Astral so that slain combatants only get soul-shocked (only, lol that shit sucks), would work really well too. You could make some good plots out of it too, like if a big Mage Arena event goes wrong and a bunch of people get soul-shocked, or key champions fall, them Seers or worse could try and take over the local consilium while everyone important is all soul-shocked and festering in hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T14:05:15-07:00","id":1343272,"title":"","content":"&quot;Jim?! Where did you send Jim, witch?!&quot;<br /> &quot;Send him? I don't underst... Oh you think I teleported him. I don't know any Space magic, leech; I can't teleport anything anywhere.&quot;<br /> &quot;Then where did he go?!&quot;<br /> &quot;Go? Where does a song go when you stop singing? Where does the light go when you unplug a lamp? Your little undead friend didn't go anywhere, vampire. I am a Master of Death! He simply stopped. He was, then he wasn't. I assure you he didn't suffer, every atom of his body, every drop of his undead essence, all annihilated at once.&quot;<br /> &quot;You.. you.. you will pay f...&quot;<br /> &quot;ENOUGH! If you don't want to suffer a similar fate you will obey!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T08:44:49-07:00","id":1343429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1343159-mage-arena?p=1343255#post1343255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage battles tend to be all or nothing. Ive very rarely had a battle last past the second round. Without rules and limitations, or a point system, like the Duel Arcane, then Mages tend to solve battles with their first spell or second spell.<br /> <br /> In my Mage setting, I actually do have a &quot;Mage Arena&quot;, led by literally just the Black Black club from Yu Yu Hakusho, Sakkyo and all, here he is a Left-Handed Seer of the Throne who has grown bored in his dominion, and uses his illegal underground monster arena and betting to entertain himself, and uses the arena as a means of punishment, execution, or even just hazing, toward other Mages, even other Seers in the case of hazing. His Arena has stone tablets that act as &quot;game modes&quot; with carefully programmed imbued effects, such as one that casts a Wards and Signs that selectively prohibits certain practices or Arcana to prevent fights ending too quickly, or at least make it harder to succeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just off the top of my head, though, I could see the Arrows forming sparring and training grounds where Mages duel each other regularly, refining the Adamant Hand or trying to integrate hurt locker merits into their Shadow Names, and such.<br /> <br /> A modified Duel Arcane system, and or hosting Mage Arena in the Astral so that slain combatants only get soul-shocked (only, lol that shit sucks), would work really well too. You could make some good plots out of it too, like if a big Mage Arena event goes wrong and a bunch of people get soul-shocked, or key champions fall, them Seers or worse could try and take over the local consilium while everyone important is all soul-shocked and festering in hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Well done, scions of Atlantis, to brave the perils of my domain and journey so deep into the Astral. Indeed I am the Morrigan, former Aeon. <br /> <br /> I know what you seek and it is still within my power to grant it. Know this, the servants of the gaol also appealed to me. But neither shall have their request, for my favor must be earned.<br /> <br /> I will call forth thine allies, your cabals and pylons. You shall relive the conflict between the hosts of the Fomorians and the Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan. To you brave souls I grant the role, power and artifacts of their greatest heroes. Thou shalt be Lugh, the Dagda, Dian Cecht, your cabal holds the right to distribute the roles as you see fit. To bring forth any resources you had in the Material, you need but think of them. No magic is forbidden. The side that tastes victory shall have their wishes granted. <br /> <br /> May your blades strike true and your deeds echo through these halls forever&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-24-2019, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}